I wrote:

[nested looting issues]

> 1. getting one's bag cursed
> 2. looting nested BoH's

Well thanks to all for the suggestions!

Funnily, most replies discussed the point (#1) I viewed as non-critical
in my post. I guess my idea about the second issue--handling nested
BoHs--seemed more or less comfortable then. It does provide the same
explosion chances as the step-by-step version and could possibly be
further rationalised along the lines of what Igor wrote in
<3ac926dc.0307071209.4f2fe16f@posting.google.com>.

As for #1, I wasn't really convinced by the ideas. They didn't seem to
provide the _proper_ balance and/or didn't fit with my logic. So how
about this:

- nested looting remains multi-turn, but takes only one turn per level

- during looting a flag (say the existing in_use flag?) is set for all
involved containers to indicate that they are open.

- curses landing on open bags/chests curse all of the items inside as
well (which may include other open bags whose items get cursed too)

this provides exactly[1] the same chances for cursing the BoH if one was
keeping it in a sack and took it out to remove something and put it back
in. It's also fairly consistent with the current state: sacks of any
kind usually protect from curses (how can a monster curse something it
cannot see?) but if they're open (and thus their contents can be seen)
everything (that is not in a closed bag) under this main inventory slot
is cursed.

I'll be gone for a week now--but I expect to release the patch a few
days after that..


till then,

Stan

-

[1]--well almost exactly. The time of exposure remains the same--two
turns, but the number of items in the main inventory would be increased
with the step-by-step version (by the BoH being there) making it a very
little bit safer.


